      "wouldReturn": 3,
      "stoppedBecause": "I reached the end of the plan: levels 181-190, after skipping the 170 boss.",
      "bestMoment": "Beating level 184 on the fifth attempt and the first time a run came out with zero leftover buckets, plus the stage-complete screen at 190.",
      "worstMoment": "Level 170 boss (5 losses over two sessions) and level 184 (4 jams before a win): leftover scraps in the 2 waiting slots decide the result and I can't see them coming. The '?' pixels never explained themselves.",
      "freeText": "Overall: nice pixel-art pictures and the paint/belt idea is clear after the first tips. But from 161 to 190 it is the same loop; I expected a new gimmick every few levels, as in the commercial match-3 games I play, and the only novelty I got was a bucket skin. The difficulty comes from jams caused by buckets that keep a few shots left and clog two slots, not from decisions that feel smart. The +1 slot saved me many times, but it is not always offered (it wasn't on the last jam in 170 and 184) and that felt arbitrary. Boss 170 felt like a wall, the levels after it much easier, which makes it feel like a spike rather than a ramp. I'd keep playing for the art, not for the puzzle."
    }
